Kasper wanted to hear about my very first afternoon.
It was a cold afternoon in January.
I stood out on the street in front of my new building.
I had two heavy suitcases.
I was very tired, and I was freezing.
I could not open the front door.
Suddenly the door opened.
A young woman came out.
She saw my suitcases and smiled broadly at me.
"Hi, my name is Nina," she said.
"I also live here in the building."
I smiled back and said my name.
Nina held the door for me.
Then she took one of the suitcases.
We carried my things inside together.
"Welcome to Denmark," Nina said.
It was my first day here.
I was happy because I already had a friend.
